  "name": "College of the Voice",
  "type": "subclass",
  "img": "modules/grimnir-lyonesse/assets/icons/skoll-sound-waves.svg",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>There are bards who speak to entertain, and there are those whose words command obedience. The College of the Voice traces its lineage to an ancient order devoted to preserving divine truth through sound. To them, the voice was not merely a gift, it was a key to the soul. Initiates are chosen young, tested for clarity of tone, memory, and self-control. They spend years in cloisters of silence, learning to still the body and discipline the mind. Through meditation and ritual speech, they master the art of persuasion so completely that their words seem to bypass reason and pierce directly into the heart. Many emerge as scholars or advisors to the powerful. Others wander the world, seeking those who might be turned toward enlightenment. Members of the College of the Voice believe that every utterance carries spiritual weight. They train to infuse their words with conviction and power. In combat, they can command enemies to falter or obey through subtle harmonics. In peace, their presence alone can sway the hearts of crowds or unravel the secrets of the unwilling. Though their order preaches humility and service, few who hear a true Voice forget the sense of awe that follows.</p>"
    },
    "source": {
      "custom": "Legends of the Round Table: Chivalric Handbook",
      "page": "42",
      "rules": "2024"
    },
